  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 344 AM EDT Mon Oct 26 2026\n\n- Cooler To Start The Week\n\nA cold front is sinking through Lower Michigan this morning and is\ncoming through dry but for a few sprinkles and increased cloud\ncover. Temperatures are getting knocked down a bit but are still\ngoing to be slightly above normal especially in southern MI. Highs\ntoday and Tue will range from the mid 50s by US-10 and mid 60s by\nI-94.\n\n- Warming Into Midweek With Showers Possible\n\nGood agreement among the ensembles for temperatures to rebound on\nWed to the upper 60s or around 70 as southwest low-level flow\nresumes on the backside of an eastern US high. High confidence in\nthese temperatures persisting into Thu, and likely through the\nweekend with perhaps a slight cooling trend. Better low- and mid-\nlevel moisture and weak lift above the warm front Tue night may\nproduce very light rain showers.\n\nA weak cold front in trail of a northern Ontario/Quebec low will\napproach the area and stall on Thursday. Models show a modest\nuptick in instability for moist parcels at 850-700 mb, so a chance\nof isolated/scattered elevated and fast-moving shower/thunderstorm\ncells is in the picture. Severe weather not expected.\n\n- Rain Chances Increase End of October into Early November\n\nEnsembles really start to diverge for Saturday into early next\nweek with shortwaves in the southern jet stream and eventual\ndeeper wave development, progression, and potential phasing of\nnorthern and southern stream waves. The main expectation is for\nprecip chances to increase, perhaps with an occasional soaking \nrainfall, though not confident for now which day or days are most\nfavored. Presently there are 20 to 30 PoPs for Halloween.",
